{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/423517-how-to-gm-a-pbp-game","id":423517,"title":"How to GM a PBP game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-28T16:01:19-08:00","id":423517,"title":"How to GM a PBP game?","content":"Somewhat what the title says. Exalted 2E is the game I'm looking to run, but I've never run a game before. I'm not sure if it would be a lost cause for me to try, as I've also never played Exalted or even a tabletop RPG. I've taken extensive notes of the relevant sections and have most of the sourcebooks. I've also done copious reading of these forums and Freedom Stone to get a feel for general fan gripes. Anyone have tips on this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5005-heavenlythunder","name":"HeavenlyThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T17:11:25-08:00","id":425803,"title":"","content":"Be open, direct and honest. You're playing on the internet, and that removes a good chunk of human communication levels. Do everything in your power to make up for that. <br /> <br /> Promote cooperation between your players. No gaming group lasts long without it. This goes doubly so for PbPs. <br /> <br /> Be patient with your players. Real life gets in the way of PbP games a lot, and that's okay. <br /> <br /> Be patient with yourself. See above.<br /> <br /> Find ways to keep your players engaged in the game, outside of the game. Throw out stories about side characters, rumors they hear in town, random bits of world building. It works wonders. <br /> <br /> Read through PbP threads, particularly ones that have lasted a long time, and ones that died shortly after launch. Try to find the common threads. Promote the behaviors you see in the long running threads while discouraging those you see in the shorter ones.<br /> <br /> Join a PbP Exalted game. Reading about the issues people have is one thing. Actually having them is another. <br /> <br /> Just go out there and do it! Your first few attempts may fail, but in many cases starting a PbP is hit-and-miss anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T18:12:10-08:00","id":425926,"title":"","content":"I agree with everything Noodle says, especially with the patience part. Part of what kills these things for me is I get all these ideas, it takes forever to proceed, and I'm burned out. However, providing asides that flesh out the area are always a way to flex your creative muscles and not rely on player input, too, which I find many players appreciate. <br /> <br /> What sort of Exalted game are you wanting to play, if I may ask?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T18:58:56-08:00","id":426023,"title":"","content":"Definitely a heroic game, though heroic would be slightly loose (enough that one need not be Superman, but not enough that Harley Quinn (depending on the writer) would be valid.) No Abyssals, and it'd have to be a veeery special Infernal to make it in. I'd probably take a few house rules that put non-Solars on a more even playing field if I got any.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5005-heavenlythunder","name":"HeavenlyThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T20:48:15-08:00","id":426124,"title":"","content":"Care to be more specific as to what you mean by heroic? Cause my &quot;Forging A Nation&quot; game here on Onyx Path, and Dietaku's &quot;To Boldly Go&quot; and &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (also here) could all be called 'heroic', but the first's a politics/bureaucracy/ Mandate of Heaven Game, the next's a Star Trek style Space Travelogue, and the last's a massive dungeon crawler. <br /> <br /> As for equalization Houserules, I would suggest using the Schaffer Lunar chargen distibution. I haven't really had issues with non-Solars keeping up with solaroids in my games, but I hear equalizing the BP costs to solar levels is a popular house rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T04:09:45-08:00","id":426419,"title":"","content":"That's why I was vague. I'm honestly up for anything and hadn't given much thought to the specific sort of game. I was going to save that until I was confident I could run one at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5005-heavenlythunder","name":"HeavenlyThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T07:01:39-08:00","id":426549,"title":"","content":"Then, I highly recommend joining an Exalted PbP, just so you know what types of games you enjoy. A game you run certainly won't last long if you don't enjoy its themes and environs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T07:32:45-08:00","id":426563,"title":"","content":"A tip that's broadly applicable to all PBP games -<br /> <br /> Get at least twice as many players as the minimum number you need in order to continue play, and be prepared to shuffle them around. Odds are that a bunch of them will drop out, likely without warning you, and possibly even before character creation is done. You'll need to reorganize those who remain. Hopefully you'll end up with a solid core of people you can depend on to write something at least twice a week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T08:40:11-08:00","id":426600,"title":"","content":"Semicasual speaks the truth. A lot of times, people will just disappear, and often not even tell you why. Such is the nature of the PbP experience, sadly. However, since you're new to tabletop RPGs, I would recommend joining a game and seeing how it works, not only to get a feel for the game, as Exalted especially has a lot of pretty weird mechanics that can overwhelm newcomers (Hello, Astrology), but also to get a feel for tabletop games in general. <br /> <br /> That being said, if you're dead set on running your own game, I'd recommend the Scavenger Lands as the Direction you set it in. There's lots of weirdness over there, gods, demons, outcaste dragonbloods, it's in the Threshold, so the Wyld Hunt isn't as powerful there, and it has the best city (Nexus), so it is a mite bit easier to ease your way into than other Directions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T11:30:19-08:00","id":426738,"title":"","content":"I agree, that'd be a good idea. Those I've encountered either have such a number of replies that I'm loath to join the frenzy, have premises I wouldn't enjoy (seafaring adventure or heavy involvement of the Underworld for instance), or use mediums/schedules I can't make use of. I'm not dead set on running one as I am being involved in one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5005-heavenlythunder","name":"HeavenlyThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T16:08:21-08:00","id":427082,"title":"","content":"If you'd like, you can join my Emerald Labyrinth game. It's set in the North, albeit in a homered section of the Haslanti League. Noodle has a nice game set in the East that we've gotten only four remaining players on, which I'm sure he'd be fine with some new blood.<br /> <br /> If you want to be a player, then, what sort of character do you wish to play?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T17:26:43-08:00","id":427139,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I'm split between an actual serious character I have or my borderline-joke one. Depends on the tone of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5005-heavenlythunder","name":"HeavenlyThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T17:30:37-08:00","id":427146,"title":"","content":"To clarify: the serious one is a former Immaculate monk turned Lunar who still believes in it. Actual potential for serious stuff. The joke one is the Solar dancer ninja rent boy. Legitimate character, but I interpret his Compassion 1, Valor 3, Conviction 3 as &quot;I do what I want regardless of the rest of you suckers&quot; so he might not mesh well on account of his... escapades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5005-heavenlythunder","name":"HeavenlyThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T18:20:01-08:00","id":427179,"title":"","content":"I play in both Noodle's game and Dietaku and I don't really think either can fit well in both games to be honest with you Heavenly thunder though the ST's are the final judge on that but in forging a nation my character will hunt immaculate monks (probably like <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nMGxqvg4K74\" target=\"_blank\">that</a>) in the near future and in the other we are trying to keep a low profile but you are free to do what you want and I will do my best to help your characters either way, you are more than welcome to join us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 03-03-2015, 09:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T20:53:48-08:00","id":427344,"title":"","content":"My character in Forging a Nation is similar to your serious idea: a black sheep of a posh household of the Ledaal family of the Realm, who exalted on a pilgrimage to prove her worthiness to Mela. The two of them would probably commiserate well on how the Realm is terrible as it is. I could see the ninja working well in Emerald Labyrinth, too, considering the...eclectic cast of characters we have. An egomaniac who uses ambush attacks and is in it for the money? That'd be some good stuff, especially considering how the Labyrinth tends to kill those with such bravado.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you're interested, then, in either, shoot me or Noodle a PM, and we'll try and help you as best as we can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T21:13:32-08:00","id":427361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/423517-how-to-gm-a-pbp-game?p=427344#post427344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're interested, then, in either, shoot me or Noodle a PM, and we'll try and help you as best as we can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ditto on that. I can see either working in my game too. <br /> <br /> Or if you'd like to start a game, I'd be happy to help as best I can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T07:49:55-08:00","id":427712,"title":"","content":"If you're still lookin', we just had some slots open up in the Whitestone Island Campaign. It's a heroic mortals game and it runs a bit slow, but we're not going anywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T10:56:37-08:00","id":427840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/423517-how-to-gm-a-pbp-game?p=427179#post427179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I play in both Noodle's game and Dietaku and I don't really think either can fit well in both games to be honest with you Heavenly thunder though the ST's are the final judge on that but in forging a nation my character will hunt immaculate monks (probably like <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nMGxqvg4K74&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">that</a>) in the near future and in the other we are trying to keep a low profile but you are free to do what you want and I will do my best to help your characters either way, you are more than welcome to join us.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the first one certainly wouldn't work. In the case of the group keeping a low profile... he would have a chance at fitting, though you would know better than I. Depends on where the game takes place, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5005-heavenlythunder","name":"HeavenlyThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T10:59:52-08:00","id":427841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/423517-how-to-gm-a-pbp-game?p=427344#post427344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My character in Forging a Nation is similar to your serious idea: a black sheep of a posh household of the Ledaal family of the Realm, who exalted on a pilgrimage to prove her worthiness to Mela. The two of them would probably commiserate well on how the Realm is terrible as it is. I could see the ninja working well in Emerald Labyrinth, too, considering the...eclectic cast of characters we have. An egomaniac who uses ambush attacks and is in it for the money? That'd be some good stuff, especially considering how the Labyrinth tends to kill those with such bravado.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you're interested, then, in either, shoot me or Noodle a PM, and we'll try and help you as best as we can.</div> </div> </div> </div>-_- Me and my piecemeal replies. Funny how that works, though\u2014our characters differ only in House and preferred Dragon. Your game is mixed-splat, then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5005-heavenlythunder","name":"HeavenlyThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T11:00:56-08:00","id":427842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/423517-how-to-gm-a-pbp-game?p=427712#post427712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're still lookin', we just had some slots open up in the Whitestone Island Campaign. It's a heroic mortals game and it runs a bit slow, but we're not going anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks very much, but I'd actually read through your campaign and I don't think it's a good fit for me. But it's extremely impressive. All the best to you in that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5005-heavenlythunder","name":"HeavenlyThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T11:07:44-08:00","id":427867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HeavenlyThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/423517-how-to-gm-a-pbp-game?p=427841#post427841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> -_- Me and my piecemeal replies. Funny how that works, though\u2014our characters differ only in House and preferred Dragon. Your game is mixed-splat, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Emerald Labyrinth is mixed splat, with every canon Exalt save a sidereal.<br /> <br /> Forging a Nation is also mixed, though Solars predominate, with 3 Solars and one Lunar as of present.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name